# Negotiation Axis-1 (Price) — Confirmed-Status Regression Guard

## Invariant (CRITICAL)

When `option_requests.status = 'confirmed'` because the model approved availability, **Axis-1 price negotiation must continue unchanged**:

- Agency: accept proposed fee, decline fee, send counter (including after client `counter_rejected`)
- Client: accept counter, decline counter, confirm job (when both axes settled)

**Forbidden:** gating price CTAs or price RPCs on `status === 'in_negotiation'` alone.

Axis-2 (availability) handlers (`agencyAcceptRequest`, model inbox) **may** keep `in_negotiation` guards — that is intentional.

## Canonical implementation (do not regress)

| Layer | Source |
|-------|--------|
| Agency D1 CTA logic | `src/utils/negotiationAgencyPriceActions.ts` |
| Client D1 CTA logic | `src/utils/negotiationClientCounterActions.ts` |
| Footer wiring | `NegotiationThreadFooter.tsx` — use helpers above, not `negotiationOpen` |
| Desktop footer | `footerTop` always renders `NegotiationThreadFooter` (ClientWeb + Agency) |
| DB RPCs | `20261328_agency_price_rpcs_post_availability_confirmed.sql` — `status IN ('in_negotiation','confirmed')` |
| Service reject fee | `agencyRejectClientPrice` — `.in('status', ['in_negotiation','confirmed'])` |

